{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains","id":122701,"title":"Hunter: Mortal Remains","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-30T15:18:47-07:00","id":122701,"title":"Hunter: Mortal Remains","content":"Hunter: Mortal Remains is out and it has a substantial Mummy chapter with two new antagonist factions of Hunters for mummies to contend with. While the book does not use the words &quot;Arisen&quot; or &quot;Deathless&quot;, the authors make it quite clear that these &quot;undying ones&quot; draw from and are inspired by Mummy: the Curse. <br /> <br /> The Faithful of Shulpae, those who eat monsters as an act of Devotion, have been discussed here previously, so I'd like to mention the new Compact: Habibti Ma. This is an Egypt based group of humans who rescue people who have fallen into cults of all kinds, but they find that they are most effective when countering the cults of charismatic god-figures. <br /> <br /> I strongly recommend this book for people who need some mortal enemies for their mummies and their cults. It even has an excellent section discussing the psychology of cultists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T15:49:39-07:00","id":122722,"title":"","content":"I'm downloading the book right now, but CAS made it clear these mummies aren't Deathless. Even in the <i>Mummy</i> core it says it's impossible to ingest a Mummy's dessicated flesh. Still, it's tempting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T16:02:47-07:00","id":122727,"title":"","content":"That comes with an interesting implication. What are these creatures, so similar to the Arisen but not? Deathless, lifeless? Where do they come from? Smells like new human AND immortal antagonists for Mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T16:07:13-07:00","id":122731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=122722#post122722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm downloading the book right now, but CAS made it clear these mummies aren't Deathless. Even in the <i>Mummy</i> core it says it's impossible to ingest a Mummy's dessicated flesh. Still, it's tempting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter exists in a neat kind of creative space, in that it draws from the mythology of the other WoD gamelines without being bound by any of the rules or canon within those books. Hunter can intentionally make Arisen/Deathless/Mummies into antagonists and it will never need to affect the vision of Mummy: the Curse. Still, I think there's quite a bit of material in Mortal Remains that can be used in a MtC game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T18:43:17-07:00","id":122834,"title":"","content":"And now Cursed Necropolis: DC has been released (to KS backers). It feels like a long drought has ended for this game! Cool thing about this book is that it comes with a map of DC and a map of the subways. Since I'm going to DC tomorrow, maybe I'll get to visit a few described locations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T09:47:12-07:00","id":123822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=122727#post122727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That comes with an interesting implication. What are these creatures, so similar to the Arisen but not? Deathless, lifeless? Where do they come from? Smells like new human AND immortal antagonists for Mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortal Remains is a Hunter: the Vigil book, so written with Hunter PCs in mind. That said...feel free to ignore us Developers as much as you want at the table. If you want 'em to be Deathless...rock out with it, if you want them to be something else...awesome.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T02:49:42-07:00","id":124384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=122722#post122722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm downloading the book right now, but CAS made it clear these mummies aren't Deathless. Even in the <i>Mummy</i> core it says it's impossible to ingest a Mummy's dessicated flesh. Still, it's tempting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The lifeless have a supernatural power to digest the power of a mummy along with the flesh but mortals having a supenatural power to digest a mummy's power with their flesh throws you for a loop?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T02:55:41-07:00","id":124387,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was rather baffled by that reasoning as well. The ability to assimilate supernatural powers isn't exactly a natural ability, and I wouldn't expect it to follow the natural laws regarding Mummy flesh.<br /> <br /> I'm planning on using the Faithful in my games, with the mechanics slightly altered so that they work more a little bit more like the Shuankhsen (the Faithful gain permanent pillars, and occasionally Affinities, by feasting on the Arisen, and can spend Pillars like Mummies in the 1-3 Sekhem ranks depending on their Status level).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T02:59:02-07:00","id":124388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=124384#post124384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lifeless have a supernatural power to digest the power of a mummy along with the flesh but mortals having a supenatural power to digest a mummy's power with their flesh throws you for a loop?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the direct contradiction of such a concept based on the <i>Mummy</i> line's developer's opinion, and the part in the core book where it says that any eaten Mummy flesh would be vomited up or otherwise not digested is what 'throws me for a loop.' Hunters, for all their endowments, are mortal, mundane, natural creatures. Shuankhsen are most definitely not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T04:17:39-07:00","id":124404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=124388#post124388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the direct contradiction of such a concept based on the <i>Mummy</i> line's developer's opinion, and the part in the core book where it says that any eaten Mummy flesh would be vomited up or otherwise not digested is what 'throws me for a loop.' Hunters, for all their endowments, are mortal, mundane, natural creatures. Shuankhsen are most definitely not</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not really buying that myself. I'm not an expert on Hunter, but Endowments are blatantly supernatural and allow for entirely unnatural benefits. A human is a mortal, mundane, natural creature, sure. As such, they should heal at a steady, natural rate. But isn't there an endowment that lets you heal wounds with a prayer? How is the ability to close a wound faster than is naturally possible any different from being able to ingest power from flesh that isn't naturally digestible? Once you're talking about magic powers, especially in a setting which already has a precedent for a certain magic power being possible (namely, Shuankhsen feasting on Arisen), saying something isn't possible because it isn't naturally possible is pretty arbitrary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T05:49:52-07:00","id":124427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=124388#post124388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the direct contradiction of such a concept based on the <i>Mummy</i> line's developer's opinion, and the part in the core book where it says that any eaten Mummy flesh would be vomited up or otherwise not digested is what 'throws me for a loop.' Hunters, for all their endowments, are mortal, mundane, natural creatures. Shuankhsen are most definitely not</div> </div> </div> </div>Well- hunters are pretty good at doing things people aren't supposed to do.. reviving the dead, for example. Or turning into a vampire. or transplanting parts of monsters into their bodies. You know, things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:16:04-07:00","id":124619,"title":"","content":"I have mixed feelings on the whole argument about the Faithful and if they are actually eating the Arisen. <br /> <br /> The fact that each game line does (if the ST wishes it to be the case) run in its own setting can mean that Hunter Mummy's and the Arisen are two separate things. The Mummy's in mortal remains are the &quot;hunterverse&quot; version of the Arisen basically.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, each game line can cross-over with others and does have some support for that idea and material to support it. I've voiced the opinion before that Mummy is the most &quot;isolated&quot; of the game lines in its fluff. Which used to bug the hell out of me but DC has gone some way to fixing that I feel, hopefully later supplements will as add more such content. <br /> <br /> Regardless you could use Arisen in a Hunter game and you could use Hunters in a Mummy game. <br /> <br /> The fact that CAS took a look at the Faithful preview posted on the Onyx Path website after a fan drew his attention to it on another thread and then basically said &quot;nope not actually the case in Mummy&quot; is simultaneously a good and bad move I feel. <br /> <br /> Its good because it upholds the idea that crossover rules relating to a major splats interaction with another gameline should only be detailed in the major splats books. A precedent Dave B has talked about in the past with the Mage/Changeling crossover rules situation that I support the idea of. <br /> <br /> It also points out an odd quirk of the Mortal Remains book. Some chapters were written by or with consultation from one of the other game lines devs or experienced writers. For example: <br /> <br /> Matt McFarland wrote the Promethean chapter, he oversaw all the Promethean splats, so he knows that setting and has a love for it and has said he'd be head dev on a Promethean Chronicle book if Onyx Path did one.<br /> <br /> Rose Bailey wrote the Demon Chapter, she's the head Dev for Demon. <br /> <br /> From what CAS has been saying he seems not to have been consulted on the Mummy chapter and the writer (while doing an excellent overall job) is not a Mummy writer veteran. Normally I would not stress this so much, but CAS has in the past mentioned he wants very particular writers for each Mummy project. <br /> <br /> On the bad side, CAS saying &quot;nope, these guys can't be doing that to the Arisen&quot; kinda undermines the idea of the Conspiracy a bit and does invalidate it within the scope of Mummy the Curse as a group that people might think have a &quot;meta&quot; validation in some way. <br /> <br /> Basically, I have the issue on a more in-theme front that Hunter Endowments are often weird supernatural powers that let people do the impossible. So why is it so hard for CAS (and by extension some fans) to imagine that an Endowment might allow for the negation/subversion of what is frankly and minor template trait? Considering their is already a president for a cannibalistic absorption of power in Mummy.<br /> <br /> It just rubs me the wrong way a little. It feels like a knee-jerk reaction/call based on OOG issue colouring an in game call.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this is all redundant anyway as each ST can make their own call on the issue thanks to the toolbox approach of the NWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:58:59-07:00","id":124650,"title":"","content":"I read that comment from CAS, and honestly...I kind of just decided to ignore it. Like you, I often see Hunters as people who, for one reason or another, have a cheat to the system(often because they are fueled by the opposition,and would anyone here be surprised if Shulpae turned out to be Ammut?), and defy the expectations. The Knights of Saint Adrian are getting so much attention because they highlight that very fact. And really, that's what Hunter's about-it's a game about how human will breaches all boundaries in the face of overwhelming adversity, even if that means burning up the individual human in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T12:09:55-07:00","id":124660,"title":"","content":"I totally agree, guys. The Mummy hunters are great inspiration for a <i>Mummy</i> game, and I know the whole World of Darkness is a sandbox, a group of puzzles whose pieces you can mix and math and that's totally how it should be. I was just relaying what CAS had said about the Faithful elsewhere (and I agree with Hawthorn about this one) in the case of completionist curiosity.<br /> <br /> In fact, don't even look at it like, &quot;Oh, you can't use the Faithful in a <i>Mummy</i> game.&quot; Interesting plots are about exceptions to the rules; we all know the Shan'iatu are dead and gone, for example, but finding the skeletal remains of one and summoning its ghost is the myth arc of my planned campaign. So look at it like, &quot;Oh, hell. How are these guys able to gain power from Mummy-flesh? What perverse arcane patrons fuel their power?&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it's been said time and time again, though, at Hunters are effectively mortal. Aside from possibly other <i>Hunter</i> supplements and developer forum posts, the side-bar of page 159 of <i>Hunter: the Vigil</i> lays it out pretty clearly that, despite the supernatural endowments they wield, Hunters are mortal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T12:11:09-07:00","id":124662,"title":"","content":"I'm putting together a &quot;master document&quot; for my next Mummy game (still ages off, I want to have Deceived, Sothis and Dreams out before I even think about writing anything about general notes) and I've decided to include the Faithful in the game. <br /> <br /> The whole Shulpae = Ammut idea is basically how I'm explaining their abilities. Though in mine I tied them to the Cult of Sobek in Egypt as an origin point. Got corrupted by some Shuankhsen then overthrew their masters during the Roman occupation...weird events were involved, the Shaunkhsen were quite shocked to be on the receiving end of cannibalism for once. <br /> <br /> (As a further explanation I'm using the Ascended Ones and keeping a lot of their fluff about the different cults in Ancient Egypt having different roles and such. In this version the Cult of Seth is not a bunch of Vampires but a brotherhood of Scorpion Sorcerers who've survived in secret up to the modern day.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T15:09:01-07:00","id":124798,"title":"","content":"nWoD's Ancient Egypt sure was a busy place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T15:16:57-07:00","id":124804,"title":"","content":"Makes sense-real world Ancient Egypt was really busy too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T16:20:06-07:00","id":124841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=124798#post124798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nWoD's Ancient Egypt sure was a busy place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Egyptian empire lasted 3,000 years.<br /> <br /> edit: For clarity purposes, 3,000 years of continuous civilization as we know it. To compare Rome (575 years for western, 1,475 for eastern) which has it's own book in the Vampire line. <br /> <br /> In short, massive amount of time in which supernaturals can get shit done and still be classified as &quot;Ancient Egyptian history&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-03-2014, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:18:46-07:00","id":124895,"title":"","content":"Another thing of note is how The Ascending Ones are now the official nemesis of the Arisen in Hunter terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T19:47:25-07:00","id":124920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=124895#post124895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing of note is how The Ascending Ones are now the official nemesis of the Arisen in Hunter terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was the AKD? The Ascending Ones may be simply more clued in on what the Arisen really are but AKD is the ones actively engages with stealing their crap left and right and thus has more practical experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T19:51:17-07:00","id":124923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=124895#post124895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing of note is how The Ascending Ones are now the official nemesis of the Arisen in Hunter terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which also probably makes them foes of the Cult of Seth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T20:59:22-07:00","id":124965,"title":"","content":"Probably not. The Remnants of Seth, as far as they (vampirically) exist, have really lost sight of what they were doing. If there's a Follower, a Khaibit, or a Hollow anywhere who was even 'alive' then(let alone remembers), they ain't steering the ship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T05:24:44-07:00","id":125129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=124798#post124798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nWoD's Ancient Egypt sure was a busy place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well lets see what was hanging out in Egypt from various game lines I'm at least passingly familiar with...<br /> <br /> Vampire - <br /> <br /> The Mekhet Clan as a whole seem to have got organized/originated in Egypt.<br /> <br /> By extension a couple of Mekhet Bloodlines (The Baka-Ra and Khaibit) trace their origin to ancient Egypt. <br /> <br /> Some of the Requiem 1.0 stuff suggests that in general Egypt was the first place that Kindred had a a society and formed Covenants. <br /> <br /> Promethean - <br /> <br /> The Osiran linage of Promethean's hails from Ancient Egypt as according to their creation myth.<br /> <br /> Hunter - <br /> <br /> The Ascended Ones used to be the Cult of Horus/Cult of the Phoenix in ancient Egypt. <br /> <br /> The Cult of Set used to be a hunter group but let themselves be turned into Vampires to fight a particularly nasty menace. They are now a Vampire organization/cult. May have been the origin point of the Khaibit Bloodline. <br /> <br /> The Faithful of Shulpae may/could have their origins here as well. <br /> <br /> Giest -<br /> <br /> Supposedly some tier 3 Krewe's had a lot of influence in Egypt and the place is full of Avernian Gates. Likely still has a decent number of Sin-Eaters in the modern day. <br /> <br /> Mummy - <br /> <br /> Obviously pre-date Ancient Egypt by a couple of thousand years (Nameless Empire lasted from about 6000BC for maybe 1000 years). However, I think Ancient Egypt and Mesopotamia were the last times that Mummy's tried to play &quot;God-King&quot; openly and the Scribes laid down the &quot;no ruling mortals openly&quot; law. <br /> <br /> Misc -<br /> <br /> The Ascended One's fluff for their alteration and the fluff in the Mekhet clan book points towards a time when a pharaoh enforced monotheism (an actual historical pharaoh did this) towards something that might have been the God Machine. Likewise he's implied to be a pretty handy sorcerer (possibly a Mage) and had a queen he &quot;hollowed out&quot; for something beyond the world to live in. Which could have been an entity of Duat, the Abyss or something from the &quot;Cults of things that should not be) from Second Sight. <br /> <br /> The new Ascended One fluff seems to point to the idea that he was possibly a Mummy and the &quot;thing&quot; in the Queen was something from Duat. However, the Mummy fluff points to the fact that this pharaoh's drive towards monotheism actually opposed the Arisen a great deal and they formed a sorta underground resistance pushing the worship of the Judges or just left Egypt. Which makes me think the Ascended Ones have got the wrong end of the stick and that the crazy pharaoh was actually a Mage dealing with the abyss, but that's just my head cannon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T08:00:49-07:00","id":125169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=124619#post124619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what CAS has been saying he seems not to have been consulted on the Mummy chapter and the writer (while doing an excellent overall job) is not a Mummy writer veteran. Normally I would not stress this so much, but CAS has in the past mentioned he wants very particular writers for each Mummy project.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's nip this is the bud right here. At the time I was contracting Mortal Remains CAS had a full slate of Mummy books to develop thanks to books already on the schedule and some bonus books added due to the Kickstarter. I asked him for recommendations for authors for the Mummy chapter of Mortal Remains and he suggested Adam, who had just contributed to Guildhalls of the Deathless. Adam had a very personal tragedy in the middle of this project so veteran Hunter writer Filamena Young (who also worked on World of Darkness: Immortals) stepped in to polish off the chapter so we could get to press.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Mortal Remains is a supplement for Hunter: the Vigil first and foremost, inspired by other game lines, but always with Hunter characters and stories as the focus of the book. I'm thrilled that people want to use elements of the book in other games, that was certainly something we were hoping for, but we built this book as part of the Hunter: the Vigil line.<br /> <br /> -Matt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T08:26:10-07:00","id":125184,"title":"","content":"That explains a lot. Thank you for sharing.<br /> <br /> Mortal Remains is actually kind of a mess on the whole, but it's still quite a powerhouse supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T09:06:14-07:00","id":125196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously pre-date Ancient Egypt by a couple of thousand years (Nameless Empire lasted from about 6000BC for maybe 1000 years). </div> </div> </div>I think you're mixing up their age with their date of creation. The First Sothic Turn was in 2371 BC, and a Sothic turn is 1461 years, so their creation would be about 3832 BC. That's only a few hundred years before the first kings of Egypt start appearing. Also that roughly coincides with the Sahara becoming a desert... Not saying there's a link there but...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T09:52:10-07:00","id":125210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=125196#post125196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're mixing up their age with their date of creation. The First Sothic Turn was in 2371 BC, and a Sothic turn is 1461 years, so their creation would be about 3832 BC. That's only a few hundred years before the first kings of Egypt start appearing. Also that roughly coincides with the Sahara becoming a desert... Not saying there's a link there but...</div> </div> </div> </div>Doh! Yeah I forgot that the Arisen were created during a Sothic Turn rather then just randomly towards the end of the Nameless Empires existence. Though Sothic Turns last a couple of hundred years right? So theoretically the Arisen could have been made over a 100 year period between the 3900's and 9800's.<br /> <br /> As far as we know at current (Deceived might change this) the Nameless Empire disappeared shortly after the Arisen were made. So we could say in the 3800BC. Which is as you say only a couple of hundred years before Ancient Egypt was a thing. <br /> <br /> So Mummy's are around 6000 years old as you say. <br /> <br /> The real question is how long did the Nameless Empire actually exist for? At current I don't feel we have enough info (once again Deceived might change this) to say for sure. A least a couple hundred years from the timeline at the front of the Mummy book, but maybe over 1000 years according to other sources such as Guildhalls and DC. If we go with the idea of the latter then the Nameless Empire was founded around 5000BC. <br /> <br /> To give some real world events from 5000BC thats around the time rice and water buffalo were domesticated in China. So the Shan'Iatu were pretty ahead of the game really. <br /> <br /> @Matt - <br /> <br /> No offense meant about the writing of the Mummy chapter. I was not in any way implying that the writer did a bad job or that this was detrimental to Mortal Remains as a book. <br /> <br /> I was simply putting together facts (or at least statements) that were previously made to try and illustrate my own conflict with a possible meta-conflict between the Hunter and Mummy's lines in regard to the Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T04:43:30-07:00","id":125717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=125210#post125210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doh! Yeah I forgot that the Arisen were created during a Sothic Turn rather then just randomly towards the end of the Nameless Empires existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes and no. It's more that their creation is the start-point to which the sothic clock is set. The actual real-life sothic calendar for egypt would flip over every time sothis' (sirius') rise corresponded to the end (or beginning, I forget) of their yearly calendar. This means that, for those purposes, a &quot;sothic turn&quot; would<br /> <br /> A) Not be a &quot;period&quot; so much as a single event, like an eclipse or a leap day<br /> B) Not particularly line up with anything interesting in the modern period (the calendar is sketchy but 2012 is definitely not one of the relevant dates).<br /> <br /> So what mummy did was declare that a &quot;sothic turn&quot; was marked as the point where sothis is in the same place (relative to the yearly calendar) that it was when any given Arisen was created. So if you were created in 3832 BC, you rise in 2371. Created in 3830? Rise 2369. And so forth. Or, put more simply, if the sothic cycle is a clock, then you don't rise when the clock reads zero, you rise when the clock reads the same &quot;number&quot; it did when you were created.<br /> <br /> So it's more that all the arisen were created within an arbitrary 100-year period, and since then they've defined a &quot;sothic turn&quot; as &quot;the point where we all start getting up&quot;.<br /> <br /> /historical rambling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 05-05-2014, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:00:18-07:00","id":125908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=125717#post125717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yes and no. It's more that their creation is the start-point to which the sothic clock is set. The actual real-life sothic calendar for egypt would flip over every time sothis' (sirius') rise corresponded to the end (or beginning, I forget) of their yearly calendar. This means that, for those purposes, a &quot;sothic turn&quot; would<br /> <br /> A) Not be a &quot;period&quot; so much as a single event, like an eclipse or a leap day<br /> B) Not particularly line up with anything interesting in the modern period (the calendar is sketchy but 2012 is definitely not one of the relevant dates).<br /> <br /> So what mummy did was declare that a &quot;sothic turn&quot; was marked as the point where sothis is in the same place (relative to the yearly calendar) that it was when any given Arisen was created. So if you were created in 3832 BC, you rise in 2371. Created in 3830? Rise 2369. And so forth. Or, put more simply, if the sothic cycle is a clock, then you don't rise when the clock reads zero, you rise when the clock reads the same &quot;number&quot; it did when you were created.<br /> <br /> So it's more that all the arisen were created within an arbitrary 100-year period, and since then they've defined a &quot;sothic turn&quot; as &quot;the point where we all start getting up&quot;.<br /> <br /> /historical rambling</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that info. I honestly did not know that their was a difference between the real world &quot;Sothic calendar&quot; and the one in Mummy. It does clarify things a little at least. I've never dug that deeply into the whole &quot;way Sothic Cycles work&quot; part of the game. I kinda just excepted them out of hand.<br /> <br /> Though until this thread I never thought about counting back 1461 years from the First Sothic Turn in the book to get the date the Arisen were starting to be made by the Shan'Iatu (3832BC). Which in retrospect seems SO obvious now. So its more likely the Arisen were made between the 3800's and 3700's then the 3900's in that case.<br /> <br /> With Irem disappearing within probably by 3600. I do hope Deceived gives us a better idea of how long Irem actually lasted. Since at the moment we have conflicting times anywhere between as short as 200 year and as much as maybe 1200 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:03:12-07:00","id":125967,"title":"","content":"Where do the 200 and 1200 years come from? Certainly not from any of the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:13:38-07:00","id":125979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/122701-hunter-mortal-remains?p=125967#post125967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do the 200 and 1200 years come from? Certainly not from any of the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit - Reread the Core book intro chapter yesterday to double check this.<br /> <br /> The 200 figure is based off the following statements in the Core Book's introduction/history section -<br /> <br /> 1) It took the Shan'Iatu 100 years to build up the City of Pillars and outfit the people that lived their for war. <br /> 2) Its stated that it took the San'Iatu something like 100 years to enact the Rite of Return on all the servants that would became Arisen.<br /> 3) Its said that the Nameless Empire only took a single year to conquer a large portion of land. However, their war with Ki-Er-Gir seems to have been quite drawn out, though no exact time scale is given. <br /> <br /> So from Core, we can count up at least 201 years of activity on part of the Nameless Empire. With a uncertain amount of time besides spent at war with Ki-Er-Gir.<br /> <br /> As for the 1200 figure that is based of a comment in DC relating to one of the NPC's memory of Irem which makes intimations that the City had been around for around a millennium by the time things started to change. I'd rounded up to 1200 because of the &quot;start up time&quot; issue that in the previous history as well. Once again, just an extrapolation from fluff.<br /> <br /> In general I don't believe that at current any hard figures relating to Irem have been published in the books directly (save that the Arisen are around 6000 years old). Its all suggested at current. Deceived might change that (hopefully).<br /> <br /> Sorry if my estimated offended, its purely infered extrapolations. I don't think I presented them as fact or anything, just a stab in the dark about estimates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 05-06-2014, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:27:53-07:00","id":126000,"title":"","content":"The Arisen also wake up variable according to their own Sothic timeline, too. Gabby said how, yes, they were all created in a hundred year span so they might not awaken according to an exact Sothic turn; but they also have a 10-30 year period of lenience even according to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mummy: the Curse, pg. 156</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever it is, it's called a Sothic turn, and it happens once every 1,461 years (give or take a decade or three) after the Mummy's life concluded.</div> </div> </div> </div>So maybe it's just me, but this is how I interpret it. The 'base' year, in the latest Sothic turn, is 2012. There's a one hundred year interval where the Mummy may have been created, which means a Mummy might awaken as early as 1962 or as late as 2062. Magic isn't perfect, though, or whatever, so any individual Mummy might wake up as early as thirty years before 1962 or as late as thirty years after 2062.<br /> <br /> So maybe, during <i>Mummy</i>'s Dark Era, there's someone who has awakened in the early 1930s (if the Dark Era goes that late). Although such an extreme case would be rare and few in number; I kind of picture the Sothic awakenings in this model as a bell curve. One might awaken in the 1930s but most will wake up in the 2000s, with some late-comers (Guildmasters?) in the mid 21st century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:41:00-07:00","id":126011,"title":"","content":"I kind of prefer the idea of the Arisen having been created all within a very short time - definitely within one year. There are certain events that have happened at the same time that are explained in the storyteller section of the Mummy book - the Shan'iatu were probably very busy when they performed the Rite of Return -, suggesting to me that this all happened in a very short period of time.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I can't imagine the Shan'iatu sacrificing thousands to empower the Rite of Return, creating the Shuankhsen in the process, and possibly sacrificing the entirety of Irem to Duat, .. and then creating the Arisen years or decades later. I find it more likely that they did this all at once.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:47:40-07:00","id":126017,"title":"","content":"Well the White Jackal mentions walking through the City and seeing it pretty much empty before he went to the Rite. Which could mean some of the stuff you mentioned before the Rite started or could have simply happened before the Jackal had his turn.<br /> <br /> Either way, we know how reliable Arisen recollection is in general. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think really its each to their own when it comes to all this time stuff really for now. Until Sothis or Deceived paints a more concrete timeline (if either does).<br /> <br /> Edit - Just realized how massively off topic we've got. <br /> <br /> As a more on topic point. While I like the Faithful of Shulpae I actually found the Habibti Ma much more evocative. I think maybe because they are a group more geared towards Cults rather then the Arisen.<br /> <br /> It was kinda nice to see a group of Hunters that are genuinely trying to do the right thing and are not necessarily being bastards about it. I also liked the general &quot;fill in the cause of this yourself&quot; element of the fact their cult deprogramming seems to work better then other peoples. Considering their tie to Ma'at I'm tempted to tie them in some way to the Heretic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 05-05-2014, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}